{
  "id": "11430_shiireru",
  "headword": "{仕入|しい}れる",
  "reading": "しいれる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to stock, to purchase for resale",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to stock, to purchase (goods for resale), to procure",
      "explanation": "To buy goods from a supplier or wholesaler for the purpose of selling them to customers. A fundamental business term in retail and commerce."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "11430_shiireru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{新鮮|しんせん}な{野菜|やさい}を{仕入|しい}れる。",
      "english": "To stock up on fresh vegetables.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11430_shiireru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{毎朝|まいあさ}{市場|いちば}で{魚|さかな}を{仕入|しい}れている。",
      "english": "Every morning I purchase fish at the market.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11430_shiireru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{海外|かいがい}から{安|やす}く{仕入|しい}れた{商品|しょうひん}をネットで{販売|はんばい}している。",
      "english": "I sell products online that I purchased cheaply from overseas.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "CONJUGATION: {仕入|しい}れる is an ichidan verb. Te-form: {仕入|しい}れて. Noun form: {仕入|しい}れ.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {商品|しょうひん}を{仕入|しい}れる (to purchase goods)\n- {仕入|しい}れ{値|ね} (purchase price, cost price)\n- {仕入|しい}れ{先|さき} (supplier, vendor)\n\nFIGURATIVE: Can also be used figuratively to mean acquiring information or knowledge: {情報|じょうほう}を{仕入|しい}れる (to gather information).",
